WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.126
For the first week after Mother left, the March sisters did remarkably well with the housework.

2
00:00:06.127 --> 00:00:11.812
They took on additional chores and made time to help each other if needed.

3
00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:15.414
Once they were relieved to know that Father was recovering,

4
00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:23.023
a great burden was lifted from their heavy hearts, and soon the girls slowly began to return to their old habits.

5
00:00:23.024 --> 00:00:31.225
Without Mother around to praise their hard work the sisters felt it only fair that they deserved a short break from their domestic chores.

6
00:00:31.226 --> 00:00:37.798
Jo caught a bad cold and was not allowed to return to Aunt March's until she was fully recovered.

7
00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:43.622
As Aunt March put it, she didn't want Jo "spreading dirty germs around the house."

8
00:00:43.623 --> 00:00:51.124
Jo had no complaints as she used the opportunity to catch up on some books that she had been aching to read.

9
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:56.996
She soon settled herself on the sofa with a warm blanket, handkerchief, and cup of hot tea.

10
00:00:56.997 --> 00:01:01.915
Amy found that additional housework had strengthened the muscles in her artist's hands,

11
00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:05.875
giving her another chance to try her skills at clay sculpting.

12
00:01:05.876 --> 00:01:15.909
Without looking back, Amy abandoned her apron for her artist's smock and before long was thumping, mashing, molding, and creating new pieces of art.

13
00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:20.751
Meg, on the other hand, faithfully continued to write to Mother and Father,

14
00:01:20.752 --> 00:01:26.733
and more often to Mr. Brookes, who she said would appreciate a warm letter from time to time.

15
00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:34.231
In fact, her evenings with paper and pen took up so much time that she was soon neglecting her household duties.

16
00:01:34.232 --> 00:01:42.359
"Amy! If you don't stop that thumping I'm going to thump your head against that table soon," Jo shouted hoarsely at her sister,

17
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:48.325
who had just destroyed a sculpture and was now trying to soften the clay to turn it into something else.

18
00:01:48.326 --> 00:01:55.753
"You're so violent and rude," snapped Amy, ignoring Jo's threats by continuing to beat the clay harder.

19
00:01:55.754 --> 00:02:00.585
"Besides, shouldn't you be in bed resting rather than down here anyway?"

20
00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:04.800
"Girls, can you keep your voices down?" said Meg irritably.

21
00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:09.689
"I'm just finishing a letter to Mother and I can't concentrate with your bickering."

22
00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:15.117
Jo childishly stuck her tongue out at Amy, who returned the gesture.

23
00:02:15.118 --> 00:02:22.793
While the others gradually ignored their chores, not to mention their consciences, Beth alone kept up her work.

24
00:02:22.794 --> 00:02:29.976
She would faithfully carry out her tasks as well as the ones her sisters had forgotten or postponed indefinitely.

25
00:02:29.977 --> 00:02:35.068
She tried to keep her spirits up by singing and humming to herself as she worked,

26
00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:42.153
imagining how wonderful it would be when Mother and Father returned home and they could be a family again.

27
00:02:42.154 --> 00:02:46.698
But as angelic as Beth was, she was also human.

28
00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:55.151
Sometimes she became so frustrated that she would seek solace in her parents' room, lying on their bed and pretending they were hugging her.

29
00:02:55.152 --> 00:03:01.936
Doing this calmed her and gave her a sense of security so that she could continue her work cheerfully.

30
00:03:01.937 --> 00:03:10.353
Beth's approach seemed to work because her sisters never saw her frowning, speaking insensitively, or acting rudely around them.

31
00:03:10.354 --> 00:03:16.036
One evening, Beth, as usual, was in the kitchen preparing a food basket for the Hummels.

32
00:03:16.037 --> 00:03:23.324
She seemed unusually tired and sighed a great deal while she slowly filled the basket with bread, fruit, and hot soup.

33
00:03:23.325 --> 00:03:28.341
When her older sisters strolled into the kitchen, Beth looked at them pleadingly and asked,

34
00:03:28.342 --> 00:03:33.808
"Would one of you be able to visit the Hummels tonight? I don't feel well."

35
00:03:33.809 --> 00:03:40.800
Meg, washing her hands, shook her head and answered, "I would if I could, but I must finish this letter to Mother.

36
00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:46.738
Then I have to write a short one to Mr. Brookes because Mr. Laurence has an urgent message for him."

37
00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:55.209
"And I can't . . . ," said Jo, forcing a cough, "because I still have this nasty cold."

38
00:03:55.210 --> 00:04:01.867
"But you seemed well enough to go out with Laurie this afternoon," Beth pointed out gently.

39
00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:10.548
Jo's face turned crimson as she replied with a chuckle, "I felt better then. But I think I should rest now."

40
00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:18.734
"I've been going every night since Mother left, but I was hoping that one of you could go instead just this once," sighed Beth.

41
00:04:18.735 --> 00:04:24.507
Meg and Jo both felt guilty that they hadn't followed Mother's instructions to visit the Hummels,

42
00:04:24.508 --> 00:04:29.384
yet they didn't want to leave their warm home and walk in the freezing cold that evening.

43
00:04:29.385 --> 00:04:34.398
In order to ease her guilt, Meg suggested, "Darling, just stay in tonight.

44
00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:41.366
I'm sure the Hummels have plenty to eat for one evening, then tomorrow I'll go and see them. I promise."

45
00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:44.972
Beth smiled at her sister and said, "Thanks, Meg.

46
00:04:44.973 --> 00:04:51.404
But since I've already filled the basket, I'll go and drop it off at their house. I'll be back shortly."

47
00:04:51.405 --> 00:04:57.160
Hugging their little sister, Meg and Jo went back to the living room to do their own thing.

48
00:04:57.161 --> 00:05:01.810
Sighing, Beth picked up the basket and got ready to leave.

49
00:05:01.811 --> 00:05:11.782
That evening the others decided to turn in early, with Meg complaining of a headache, Jo blaming her cold, and Amy wanting her beauty sleep.

50
00:05:11.783 --> 00:05:18.489
Soon after Jo had fallen asleep, however, she was awakened by slow footsteps creeping up the stairs.

51
00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:25.143
Alarmed, she silently got out of bed, careful not to disturb her sleeping sisters.

52
00:05:25.144 --> 00:05:32.412
The footsteps stopped in front of her parents' room, so Jo cautiously tiptoed over and slowly opened the door.

53
00:05:32.413 --> 00:05:36.419
What she saw frightened her more than anything she could imagine.

54
00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:43.964
"Beth! Beth! What happened?" she cried, seeing her sister spread out on their parents' bed.

55
00:05:43.965 --> 00:05:48.370
Beth was breathing unevenly and her face was flushed with fever.

56
00:05:48.371 --> 00:05:54.774
Panicking, Jo looked around for a washcloth and water to cool Beth's burning face.

57
00:05:54.775 --> 00:05:58.151
"Jo?" Beth whispered weakly.

58
00:05:58.152 --> 00:06:03.940
"I'm right here, darling," Jo replied, placing a wet washcloth on Beth's forehead.

59
00:06:03.941 --> 00:06:08.488
"Jo? She died . . . " Beth's voice broke.

60
00:06:08.489 --> 00:06:13.013
"Who, Beth? Who died?" Jo asked, startled at her words.

61
00:06:13.014 --> 00:06:20.019
"The baby, Hummels' baby . . . in my arms . . . ," Beth managed to say.

62
00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:25.614
"Oh, my poor darling," Jo cried, holding Beth close to her.

63
00:06:25.615 --> 00:06:36.860
"Doctor said . . . scarlet . . . scarlet fever . . . all the children have it . . . ," continued Beth. "Jo? I might be sick too."

64
00:06:36.861 --> 00:06:41.217
Jo's heart sank and she wanted to scream aloud with anguish.

65
00:06:41.218 --> 00:06:49.498
Scarlet fever, as everyone knew in those days before antibiotics and childhood immunizations, was often fatal.

66
00:06:49.499 --> 00:06:55.160
Both Meg and Jo had already had the disease and so their bodies were immune to the bacteria.

67
00:06:55.161 --> 00:07:01.371
Amy, on the other hand, had never had scarlet fever, which was both contagious and dangerous.

68
00:07:01.372 --> 00:07:07.640
"I wish I knew what to do!" cried Jo, beating her fists against the bed in frustration.

69
00:07:07.641 --> 00:07:14.591
"Please, Jo, my throat is so dry . . . my head hurts . . . ," Beth mumbled weakly.

70
00:07:14.592 --> 00:07:21.939
Clutching her sister, Jo wept loudly, hating herself for allowing Beth to go to the Hummels when she should have gone,

71
00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:26.535
and at the same time, wishing Mother were there to tell her what to do.

72
00:07:26.536 --> 00:07:35.579
"Jo? Keep Amy away. Keep her away . . . ," said Beth before she closed her eyes and became silent.

